  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The test covers every scenario in the example and asserts the expected outcomes.\n\n**Test.** `missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence` in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` carries the `{test}` reference to `requirements.authoring.submission_count`. It runs a mock Ollama server that returns one canned reply, and it covers these cases:\n- **No tool calls.** `vec![]` gives a reply with only the prose \"review complete\", so the model never calls `submit_judgment`.\n- **Two identical submissions.** Two `submit_judgment` calls carry the same valid payload.\n- **One invalid submission.** A single call has an empty rationale. A second single call has `{\"FIXME\": []}` as its determination, which is also invalid.\n\nEach case runs twice, once writing to the evidence file and once with `--stdout`. After each run the test asserts:\n- The exit status is a failure.\n- `stdout` is empty.\n- The evidence file is byte-identical to the original.\n- The usage record has `outcome == \"failed\"`, `evidence_written == false`, and a null determination.\n- `request_count == 1`, so no replacement submission was requested and there is no repair loop.\n- The server's `finish()` runs, which joins the server thread. The mock was built with exactly one reply.\n\n**Implementation.** `assess` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` carries the `{impl}` reference.\n- **Prose only.** If there are no tool calls, it returns the error \"model finished without invoking submit_judgment\".\n- **Multiple submissions.** If `submissions.len() != 1`, it returns an error before accepting either one, and the payloads are never compared, so identical payloads still fail.\n- **Invalid arguments.** `submission(...)` rejects empty rationales, bad judgments, and wrong field sets, and `result?` returns the error immediately. The loop does not continue, so the model is not asked again.\n- **No evidence on failure.** Evidence is built and returned only on the success path, so the failure paths write none.\n\nThe test matches the implementation, so the example is covered.",
